sentences.l:
And now still more Paeonians would swift Achilles have killed,
if the river, deep-eddying, had not, incensed, addressed him,
having made himself like a man, and from the deep eddy called out:

and he, out of the eddy having sprung up,
darted over the plain, on rushing feet to fly,
in fear;

And Peleus’-son sprang away as far as the rush of a spear reaches,
with the rush of an eagle, the black one, the hunter,
which is at once the strongest and the swiftest of winged things;

And as when a man, a channel-leader, from a dark-watered spring
through plants and gardens guides the flow with water,
having a mattock in his hands, casting the obstructions out of the ditch;

not to stop your hands from the war common to all
before within Ilios’ famous walls the Trojan people
you have hemmed in, whoever flees;
